A language spoken in many countries. We are speaking it 
{{wikipedia}}
{{interwiktionary|en}}
{{BNC1HW|enjoy|engine}}

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{enPR|ĭng'glĭsh}}
* {{IPA|/ˈɪŋglɪʃ/}}
* {{SAMPA|/"INglIS/}}
* {{audio|en-us-English.ogg|US}}

== Proper noun ==
{{proper noun}}
# '''English''' is a [[language]] spoken by around 800 [[million]] people. The main places where '''English''' is spoken include:
#* The [[United Kingdom]] and [[Ireland]]
#* The [[United States of America|United States]] and [[Canada]]
#* [[India]], [[Pakistan]], [[Australia]] and all the other {{r|countr|ies}} of the old [[British Empire]].
# {{surname}}

== Adjective ==
{{adj|more=true}}
# The '''English''' refers to the [[people]] who live in [[England]].
#: ''The '''English''' don't care for people like that.''
# Something that is '''English''' is related to [[England]], its [[people]] or its [[culture]].
#: ''I prefer the '''English''' accent.''
#: ''I am '''English'''.''

=== Related words ===
* [[language]]
* [[British]]
* [[American]]

[[Category:Languages]]
[[Category:Nationalities]]
[[Category:Terms suffixed with -ish]]
[[Category:English| ]]

{{wikipedia}}

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdɪkʃən(ə)ri/}}, {{SAMPA|/"dIkS@n(@)ri/}}
* {{US}} {{enPR|dĭk'shə-nĕr"ē}}, {{IPA|/ˈdɪkʃənˌɛri/}}, {{SAMPA|/"dIkS@n%Eri/}}
* {{audio|en-uk-dictionary.ogg|UK}}
* {{audio|en-us-dictionary.ogg|US}}

== Noun ==
{{noun|2=dictionaries}}
[[File:Blacks-Law-Dictionary.jpg|thumb|A '''dictionary'''.]]
[[File:BilingualDictionaries.jpg|thumb|Some [[bilingual]] '''dictionaries'''.]]
# {{countable}} A '''dictionary''' is a [[book]] that tells you what [[word]]s mean, and how to [[spell]] them. A lot of '''dictionaries''' will also tell you about [[etymology]] (where words come from) and [[pronunciation]] (how to speak them). {{syn|lexicon|wordbook}}
#: ''You are reading an online '''dictionary''' right now.''
#: ''The words in a printed '''dictionary''' are in [[alphabetical order]].''
#: ''I looked up the '''dictionary''' to find the meaning of the word [[business]].''

=== Related words ===
* [[definition]]
* [[diction]]
* [[thesaurus]]
* [[reference]]

[[Category:Dictionaries|Dictionaries]]

=== Other spellings ===
* [[encyclopaedia]]
{{wikipedia}}

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{CA}} {{IPA|/ənˌsəɪ.kləˈpi.di.ə/}}
* {{UK}} {{US}} {{IPA|/ɪnˌsaɪ.kləˈpi(ː).di.ə/}}
* {{audio|en-us-encyclopedia.ogg|US}}
* {{hyph|en|cy|clo|pe|di|a}}

== Noun ==
{{noun|3=encyclopediae}}
[[File:Encyclopedia Britannica.jpg|thumb|Some books of an '''encyclopedia''']]
# {{countable}} An '''encyclopedia''' is a type of [[book]] that has [[information]] about various [[thing]]s. Often, an '''encyclopedia''' is a [[set]] of many books and can either be about a [[specific]] [[subject]] or a [[range]] of subjects.
#: ''[[Wikipedia]] is an online '''encyclopedia''' and is the world's largest.''
#: ''I went to the [[library]] to find an '''encyclopedia''' on [[chemistry]].''

=== Related words ===
* [[encyclopedic]]

[[Category:Reference works]]

==Translingual==

{{letter|A}}

===Uppercase===

# ([[typography]]) a [[capital]] a.

===Lowercase===

# ([[typography]]) a [[lowercase]] a.
# ([[phonetics]]) an [[open]] [[front]] [[unrounded]] [[vowel]].

==English==

{{BE850}}
{{BNC1HW}}
{{wikipedia}}

=== Pronunciation ===
; {{q|letter name}}
* {{UK}} {{US}} {{IPA|/eɪ/}}
* {{AU}} {{IPA|/æɪ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-a.ogg|US}}
* {{audio|en-us-A.ogg|US}}
* {{audio|en-uk-a.ogg|UK}}

=== Determiner ===
{| border=0 width=100%
|-
|bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=49%|
Determiner<br />
'''a'''
|bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=49%|
Before vowel sounds<br />'''[[an]]'''
|}
# {{det|s|c}} '''A''' is used when you don't expect your listener to identify which thing you mean. {{syn|one|any|each}}
#: ''Compare "'''A''' book I saw on the shelf" and "'''The''' book I gave you yesterday".''

=== Note ===
* If the following word starts with a [[vowel]] sound, then we use [[an]] instead.
* It is called the [[indefinite article]].
* It is not used in the plural: ''a book'' → ''books'' but not <s>''a books''</s>.

== Noun ==
{{letter|A}}
[[File:Latin A.png|thumb|The letter '''A''']]
# '''A''' is the [[first]] [[letter]] of the [[alphabet]].
#: ''The letter '''"a"''' comes before "b".''
# {{context|school}} In some schools, an '''A''' is a very high grade.
#: ''Ron got an '''A''' on his earth science test.''

{{alphabet}}

[[Category:Determiners]]
[[Category:Articles]]

{{BNC1HW}}

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɪmpl/}}
* {{audio|en-us-simple.ogg|US}}
* {{audio|en-uk-simple.ogg|UK}}
* {{hyph|sim|ple}}

== Adjective ==
{{adj|simple|simpler|simplest}}
# A '''simple''' task is [[easy]] to do and easy to understand. {{syn|easy|basic|plain|uncomplicated}} {{ant|complicated|complex|difficult|sophisticated}}
#: ''Baking this cake is very '''simple''' as it only has 3 steps.''
#: ''It's a '''simple''' book for learners to read and understand.''
# Something that is '''simple''' is [[basic]] and not [[complicated]]. {{syn|basic|plain|uncomplicated}} {{ant|complicated|complex|sophisticated}}
#: ''She was poor and only had a '''simple''' dress.''
#: ''Their plan was very '''simple'''.''
# A '''simple''' person is not [[intelligent]] (we sometimes use this in a bad way) {{syn|unintelligent}} {{ant|intelligent|artful}}
#: ''He isn't a bad boy, he's just a little '''simple'''.''
# In grammar, the '''simple''' [[aspect]] is used when the speaker sees the situation as [[complete]] (compare [[progressive]] aspect).
#: ''"I run" is the present '''simple'''; "I'm running" is the present progressive.''

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# {{old}} {{medicine}} A '''simple''' is a [[medicine]] that is [[prepare]]d only from one [[plant]].

== Verb ==
{{verb|simpl|e}}
# {{ti verb}} {{medicine}} When you '''simple''' things (especially [[herb]]s), you are trying to [[gather]] [[#Noun|simples]].

=== Related words ===
* [[simplex]]
* [[simply]]
* [[simplify]]
* [[simplicity]]

{{wikipedia}}
{{BE850}}
{{BNC1HW}}

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{UK}} {{IPA|/wɜːd/}}, {{SAMPA|/w3:d/}}
* {{US}} {{enPR|wûrd}}, {{IPA|/wɝd/}}, {{SAMPA|/w3`d/}}
* {{audio|en-us-word.ogg|US}}
{{-}}
== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# '''Words''' are the smallest [[meaningful]] pieces of a [[language]] that can be used on their own.
#: ''Do you even understand the '''words''' I am saying?!''
#: ''Class, if you are not [[sure]] on any '''word''', be sure to check the [[dictionary]].''
# A '''word''' is a short [[conversation]].
#: ''Can I have a '''word''' with you, John?''
#: ''Mr. Gambini, a '''word''' with you, please?''
# A '''word''' is a [[promise]] given to someone.
#: ''She gave him her '''word''' that she would pay him the money on Tuesday.''
#: ''You have my '''word''' for it that the work will be finished before the weekend.''
# A '''word''' is a piece of [[news]].
#: ''Send '''word''' to John that Mary is here.''
#: ''The '''word''' is that Mary stole some money from John.''
# When [[Christian]]s speak about the [[Bible]], they sometimes call it the '''Word'''. {{syn|Bible}}

== Verb ==
{{verb}}
# {{transitive}} When you '''word''' something, you are trying to [[say]] or [[write]] it using certain [[#Noun|words]] and to [[phrase]] it in a certain way. {{syn|express|phrase|put into words|state}}
#: ''The mayor's [[speech]] was carefully '''worded''' to avoid [[offend]]ing the [[angry]] [[protester]]s.''

[[Category:Language]]
[[Category:Religion]]
[[Category:Autological words]]

{{BE850}} {{BNC1HW}}
=== Pronunciation === * {{UK}} {{enPR|hwĕn}}, {{IPA|/ʍɛn/}}, {{SAMPA|/WEn/}} * {{US}} {{enPR|wĕn|hwĕn}}, {{IPA|/wɛn/|/ʍɛn/}}, {{SAMPA|/wEn/|/WEn/}} * {{audio|en-us-when.ogg|US}} * {{audio|en-ne-when.ogg|US}} * {{audio|en-uk-when.ogg|UK}}
== Preposition == {{preposition}} # at what time; on what occasion #: ''"'''When''' did you start learning English?" – "Three years ago."'' #: ''"'''When''' does the film start?" – "At seven o'clock."'' #: '''''When''' was the last time you went to your local library?'' # at the time #: ''She phoned me '''when''' I was in the bath.'' #: ''It was the year 1996 '''when''' I met John.'' # after #: '''''When''' I get up, I always drink a cup of coffee.''
=== Related words === * [[then]] * [[whenever]]
[[Category:Time]] [[Category:Relative prepositions]] [[Category:Interrogative prepositions]] [[Category:Prepositions with clause complements]] [[Category:Intransitive prepositions]]

=== Pronunciation === * {{UK}} {{IPA|/bɪˈlɒŋ/}}, {{SAMPA|/bI"lQN/}} * {{US}} {{enPR|bĭ-längʹ}}, {{IPA|/bɪˈlɑŋ/}}, {{SAMPA|/bI"lAN/}} * {{audio|en-us-belong.ogg|US}}
== Verb == {{verb}} # {{intransitive}} If <math>x</math> '''belongs''' to <math>y</math>, it is <math>y</math>'s #: ''The [[umbrella]] '''belongs''' to John; it's his.'' # {{intransitive}} If someone '''belongs''' to something like a club, they are a [[member]]. #: ''Mary '''belongs''' to Greenpeace.'' #: ''What does it cost to '''belong''' to the library?'' #: ''English '''belongs''' to the [[Indo-European]] language family.'' # {{intransitive}} If something '''belongs''', it is in the [[right]] [[place]]. #: ''That dog doesn't '''belong''' in the kitchen.'' #: ''Where does this book '''belong'''?'' #: ''I'm a simple girl; I don't '''belong''' in this rich house.''
=== Related words === * [[belongings]]

=== Pronunciation ===
;verb
* {{a|stressed}} {{enPR|dŭz}}, {{IPA|/ˈdʌz/}}, {{SAMPA|/ˈdVz/}}
* {{a|unstressed}} {{IPA|/dəz/}}, {{SAMPA|/d@z/}}
* {{audio|en-us-does-todo.ogg|Audio (US)}}

;noun
* {{enPR|dōz}}
* {{IPA|/dəʊz/}}
* {{SAMPA|/d@Uz/}}
