==Verb== {{verb3|be|am|is|are|was|were|been|being}} {| border=0 width=100% |- |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| '''Negatives:''' | width=0.5% | |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| None, '''[[isn't]], [[aren't]]''' | width=0.5% | |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| '''[[wasn't]], [[weren't]]''' | width=0.5% | |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| None | width=0.5% | |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| None |} {| border=0 width=100% |- |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| '''Contractions:''' | width=0.5% | |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| '''[['m]], [['s]], [['re]]''' | width=0.5% | |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| None | width=0.5% | |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| None | width=0.5% | |bgcolor="#e2e2ff" valign=top width=20% style="padding-left:1em;"| None |} # {{Auxiliary}} {{linking verb}} A form of the [[verb]] ''[[be]]'' used about the person you are talking to. #: ''Only you '''were''' doing it right.'' # {{Auxiliary}} {{linking verb}} A form of the verb ''be'' used about more than one person. #: ''We '''were''' going home.'' #: ''You all '''were''' staying late.'' #: ''They '''were''' all playing in the band.'' # {{Auxiliary}} {{linking verb}} A form of the verb ''be'' used with the word [[if]]. #: ''If I '''were''' rich, I would retire.'' # {{Auxiliary}} {{linking verb}} A form of the verb ''be'' used about things you wish for. #: ''I wish it '''were''' the weekend.''
===Note=== * In the last two examples, many people use ''[[was]]'' instead.
[[Category:Auxiliary verbs]]

