{{shortcut|[[WT:A]]<br>[[WT:ADMIN]]<br>[[WT:SYSOP]]<br>[[WT:MOP]]}}
'''Administrators''', also called '''admins''' or '''sysops''' ('''sys'''tem '''op'''erator'''s'''), are editors that have access to special features that help keep Wiktionary running well.  They have access to these features because they are trusted by the community, but this does not make them better or more important than anybody else.

== Things they can do ==
[[File:Wiktionary Administrator.svg|thumb|This is the symbol of administrators. It shows the site's logo with a [[mop]], because administrators can be thought of as Wiktionary's [[janitor]]s.]]
* [[Wiktionary:Deletion|Delete]] pages
** Requests should be made at [[Wiktionary:Requests for deletion]] unless a page can be [[Wiktionary:Deletion#Quick deletion|quick deleted]].
* [[Wiktionary:Protection|Protect]] and unprotect pages and edit protected pages, including those in the [[:en:Wikipedia:MediaWiki namespace|MediaWiki namespace]].
** Requests can be made at [[Wiktionary:Administrators' noticeboard]]. Please remember that pages are usually protected when there is vandalism or an edit war is in process, and not to prevent vandalism.
* [[Wiktionary:Bans and blocks|Block]] disruptive users
** Requests should be made at [[Wiktionary:Administrators' noticeboard]], but only if the user has been disruptive.  Requests made in [[Wiktionary:Assume good faith|bad faith]] may result in you yourself being blocked.
* Rollback changes
** Administrators can rollback all changes by a user and it is automatically marked as minor and gives the following edit summary:

:::''Reverted changes by '''User A''' ('''talk''') to last version by '''User B''' <small>([[Special:Tags|Tag]]: Rollback)</small>''

== Bureaucrats ==
{{shortcut|[[WT:BUR]]<br>[[WT:CRAT]]<br>[[WT:BCRAT]]<br>[[WT:BUREAUCRAT]]}}
A '''bureaucrat''' is a slightly higher administrative level than ''sysop'' and can perform a few additional functions. Bureaucrats can give and remove sysop permission and grant bureaucrat status to other users after a successful request. They can also "flag" [[Wiktionary:Bots|bots]], which hides a user's contributions from the [[Special:RecentChanges|new changes]] and puts them in the bot group.

Prior to 15 September 2014, bureaucrats could rename users locally on their project. That function has then been disabled and a historic log of those actions can be found [[Special:Logs/renameuser|here]].

Renames should now be requested using [[Special:GlobalRenameRequest|this special page]].

== Requesting adminship ==
Please see [[Wiktionary:Requests for permissions|the request for permissions page]] to nominate yourself or another user for administrator or bureaucrat status.

