== Determiner == {{determiner}} # {{det|s|c}} {{lc|Any}} one out of two [[option]]s. #: ''I can [[write]] with '''either''' [[hand]].'' #: ''You can drink '''either''' tea or coffee.'' #: ''They can be used '''either''' alone or in groups.'' #: ''Few people liked it; most '''either''' ignored it or hated it.'' # {{det|b=definite|s|c}} {{lc|Each}} or [[both]] from two options. #: ''The room has a door at '''either''' end.'' #: ''People were walking on '''either''' side of the road.'' #: ''I can't [[find]] '''either''' shoe. I have [[lost]] both shoes.'' #: ''I have a blue [[coat]] and a green coat. '''Either''' will keep me [[warm]].'' #: ''There will still be problems in '''either''' of the following two cases.''
== Adverb == {{adv}} # Used in negative [[statement]]s to mean ''[[too]]'' or ''[[also]]''. {{syn|or|any}} {{ant|neither}} #: ''I don't [[like]] him and I don't like her '''either'''.'' #: ''I can't [[sing]] and I can't [[dance]] '''either'''.'' #: ''No other country has any real friends '''either'''.''
=== Usage notes === * You use '''either''' to pick out one of two choices when it does not matter which one is chosen. When faced with more than two choices, you should use ''[[any]]''.

