== Determiner == {{determiner}}{{rel det}} # {{det|b=definite}} {{context|question}} You use '''whichever''' when it doesn't matter which thing. #: '''''Whichever''' colour you choose, you'll be happy.'' # {{det|b=definite}} {{context|relative}} You use '''whichever''' when it doesn't matter which thing. {{synonyms|any}} #: ''It's OK to take '''whichever''' bus comes first.'' #: '''''Whichever''' of these two wins will take first prize.'' #: ''"Would you like the blue or the green?" "Oh, '''whichever''' colour, it doesn't matter."'' # {{det|b=definite}} {{context|relative, definite}} You use '''whichever''' when there's a particular thing, but you can't remember what it was. #: ''We took '''whichever''' bus came first, number 41 I think.''
== Pronoun == {{pronoun}} # {{context|question}} You use '''whichever''' when it doesn't matter which thing. #: '''''Whichever''' you choose, you'll be happy.'' # {{context|relative, indefinite}} You use '''whichever''' when it doesn't matter which thing. {{synonyms|any}} #: ''It's OK to take '''whichever''' comes first.'' #: '''''Whichever''' of these two wins will take first prize.'' #: ''"Would you like the blue or the green?" "Oh, '''whichever''', it doesn't matter."'' # {{context|relative, definite}} You use '''whichever''' when there's a particular thing, but you can't remember what it was. #: ''We took '''whichever''' came first, number 41 I think.''

