== Adjective == {{adj}} # {{attrib}} If something is your '''own''' it [[belong]]s to you or is about you (often used for emphasis). #: ''I wish I had my '''own''' home.'' #: ''I bought it in my '''own''' name.'' #: ''The toy began to move as though it had a life of its '''own'''.'' #: ''accidents happen, and often in your very '''own''' home. '' # If you are on your '''own''', you are by yourself, there is no body else with you. This can also mean there is no one helping you. #: ''I was on my '''own''' in the woods.'' #: ''If you try to do that you're on your '''own''' – or at least I won't help you!''
=== Usage === * In almost all cases, '''own''' must follow a [[possessive]]. *: ''She lives in <u>her</u>'' (not: ''<u>an</u>'')'' '''own''' house.'' *: ''He repeated the <u>president's</u> '''own''' words.'' (not: ''He repeated <u>the</u> '''own''' words.'') * There are a very small number of set phrases, such as ''an '''own''' goal'', in which '''own''' doesn't need to follow a possessive.
== Verb == {{verb}} # If you '''own''' something it belongs to you, it is [[yours]]. #: ''Yes, I '''own''' a car.'' #: ''I plan to build a house on the land I '''own'''.'' # If you ''"'''own''' up"'' to something, you admit you did it. #: ''I had to '''own''' up to lying about our relationship.''

