== Adjective == {{adjective}} # Just one or just a few; this and no other; no more than this. #: ''She is the '''only''' woman doctor in this city.'' #: ''These are the '''only''' coins I have.'' # {{attrib}} An '''only''' [[child]], [[son]], girl, etc. has no [[brother]]s or [[sister]]s.
== Preposition == {{preposition}} # {{informal}} You use '''only''' to introduce a fact that prevents a statement from being completely true. {{syn|except|but}} #: ''They probably could do it, '''only''' you never let them try.''

