# If something is '''abstract''', you cannot [[touch]] it, and it is difficult to [[imagine]] or [[think]] about. {{syn|abstruse}}
#: ''A lot of '''abstract''' painting uses harsh shapes and most people do not like it.''
#: ''More '''abstract''' ideas like "democracy" are not possible for animals.''
#: ''Houses and books are things you can touch.  Honesty, patience and courage are '''abstract'''.''
# {{context|logic}} If something is '''abstract''', it is [[general]]. {{syn|general}} {{ant|particular}}
# If something is '''abstract''', it is thought of as apart from any other use with an [[object]]; it is [[removed]] from it; it is [[separate]] or [[abstracted]]. {{syn|removed|separate}}
# If something is '''abstract''', it is not [[practical]] or [[realistic]]; it is not [[concrete]]; it is [[theoretical]]; it is [[vague]]. {{syn|vague|theoretical}} {{ant|applied|practical|realistic|concrete}}
# If something is '''abstract''', it does not have all of the [[fact]]s; it is not [[factual]]. {{syn|formal}} {{ant|factual}}

=== Related words ===
* [[abstractly]]
* [[abstractness]]

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# {{countable}} An '''abstract''' is a short [[text]] that tells you the main ideas of a longer text, especially of scientific papers; it is a [[summary]] of something longer. {{syn|summary|synopsis|epitome}}
#: ''The '''abstract''' of Isaac Newton's laws of gravity may be no more than 150 words.''
# {{countable}} An '''abstract''' is an [[abstraction]]; it is an '''abstract''' [[word]].
# {{countable}}; {{context|art}} An '''abstract''' is a piece of [[art]] that is made in the '''abstract''' fashion of art.
# {{countable}}; {{medicine}} An '''abstract''' is a [[powdered]] solid [[extract]] of a [[vegetable]] that is then mixed with the sugar of [[milk]].

=== Related words ===
* [[abstraction]]

== Verb ==
{{verb}}
# {{transitive}} If you '''abstract''' something, you [[summarize]] it; you [[abridge]] it.
# {{transitive}} If you '''abstract''' something, you [[separate]] it; you [[remove]] it.
# {{transitive}} If you '''abstract''' something, you [[withdraw]] it.
# {{transitive}}; {{context|art}} If you '''abstract''' something, you make [[abstraction]]s of it in [[art]].
# {{transitive}}; {{context|euphemistic}} If you '''abstract''' something, you take it away from someone without [[permission]]; you [[steal]] it. {{syn|filch|purloin|steal}}
# {{transitive}} If you '''abstract''' something, you think about it separate from everything else; you [[consider]] it [[abstractly]].
# {{intransitive}}; {{rare}} If you '''abstract''' something, you go through the [[process]] or [[abstraction]].

