== Verb == {{verb2|hold|holds|held|held|holding}} [[File:Smiling woman holding a cup of beer.jpg|thumb|a woman '''holding''' (''sense 1'') a [[cup]]]] [[File:Felicitas in de gevangenis met de cipier, objectnr A 41865.tif|thumb|a [[guard]] '''holding''' (''sense 2 and 5'') a [[prisoner]]]] # {{transitive}} When you '''hold''' something, you put it in your [[hand]] and keep it there. #: ''He '''held''' the pen [[tight]]ly as he [[wrote]] the [[letter]].'' # {{transitive}} When you '''hold''' something, you [[keep]] it in one place and do not let it move away. #: ''The [[police]] '''hold''' people who do [[crime]]s in [[prison]].'' # {{transitive}} If you '''hold''' someone accountable/responsible/liable, you put the responsibility for something on them. #: ''It's not clear if parents should be '''held''' responsible for the problems their children cause.'' #: ''We are trying to finally get tobacco companies '''held''' responsible for killing people.'' # {{intransitive}} If something '''holds''' true/good, it is or continues to be true. #: ''The drug extends life for mice. If this '''holds''' true in humans as well, it will be a great advance.'' #: ''He might be able to do it, but I don't think that '''holds''' for most men.'' # {{transitive}} If you '''hold''' somebody prisoner/hostage/captive, you do not allow them to go free. #: ''Police in Luxembourg say a gunman '''holding''' 29 children hostage is demanding a mini-bus to take him to the airport.''

