== Verb == {{verb}} # {{transitive}} If <math>x</math> concerns <math>y</math>, <math>x</math> is about <math>y</math>. #: ''We have received a letter that '''concerns''' the recent sale of the property.'' #: ''The article is primarily '''concerned''' with Dylan's early life.'' # {{transitive}} If something '''concerns''' a person, they think it is a problem or needs [[attention]]. #: ''The recent losses certainly '''concern''' me, but I still think things are looking good.'' # You use ''to whom it may '''concern''''' at the beginning of a letter when you don't know the name of the person you're writing to.

