==Suffix== {{suffix}} # '''n't''' is used to [[negate]] a [[clause]].
===Usage notes=== The suffix '''-n't''' can only be added to [[auxiliary verb]]s (also called [[helping verb]]s). The resulting word usually means the same thing as the verb plus ''not'' (for example, ''don't'' means ''do not'', ''won't'' means ''will not''). Some verbs change their spelling when '''-n't''' is added (for example, ''shall'' becomes ''shan't'') and some verbs do not accept '''-n't''' (for example, ''am'').
