== Noun == {{noun}} # {{countable}} A '''career''' is a [[job]] or a series of related jobs that you do for many years. #: ''His pro coaching '''career''' spans 23 years, including time with the 49ers (1967–73 and' 77), the Browns (1978–80), the Oilers (1981–82), the Cowboys (1983–85) and the Cardinals (1986–89).'' #: ''She says that she enjoyed making the movie, but has no plans to pursue an acting '''career'''.'' #: ''Students need more support from teachers and advisers in deciding about academic programs and '''career''' paths.'' #: ''Don quit his old job and launched a new '''career''', restoring classic cars in a backyard garage.'' #: ''He lost his hand in an accident, which ended his painting '''career'''.'' #: '''''Career''' advancement is often based on job performance, not just how long you've been in the job.''
