{{documentation subpage}}
<!-- Categories, interwikis and TemplateData go at the bottom of this page. -->
This template is used as a part of speech header for [[verb]]s.

== Usage ==
<pre>
{{verb
| 1 = Plain form
| 2 = Third-person singular
| 3 = Past tense
| 4 = Past particle
| 5 = Present participle
}}
</pre>
Note: <code><nowiki>{{{2}}}</nowiki></code> may be used for short-cuts as explained in the [[#Examples|examples]] below.

== Examples ==
;Regular verbs
For regular verbs, use <code><nowiki>{{verb}}</nowiki></code> to make:
{{verb}}

;Different plain form (usually used for derived word forms)
To use a different verb from the pagename, use <code><nowiki>{{verb|talk}}</nowiki></code> to make:
{{verb|talk}}

;Verbs ending with "e"
For most regular verbs ending in e, use <code><nowiki>{{verb|bak|e}}</nowiki></code> to make:
{{verb|bak|e}}

;Verbs ending with "y"
For most regular verbs ending in y, use <code><nowiki>{{verb|hurr|y}}</nowiki></code> to make:
{{verb|hurr|y}}

;Verbs with double consonants
For most regular verbs with a double consonant (a letter that is sometimes there one time and sometimes two times) use <code><nowiki>{{verb|grip|p}}</nowiki></code> to make:
{{verb|grip|p}}

;Regular verbs that add "es"
For most regular verbs that add "es" because they end in a sound like "s", "sh", "ch", etc., use <code><nowiki>{{verb|push|es}}</nowiki></code> to make:
{{verb|push|es}}

;Other verbs
For other regular verbs, (any verb where past tense and past participle are the same) use <code><nowiki>{{verb|agree|agrees|agreed|agreeing}}</nowiki></code> to make:
{{verb|agree|agrees|agreed|agreeing}}

;Irregular verbs
For irregular verbs, use <code><nowiki>{{verb|take|takes|took|taken|taking}}</nowiki></code> to make:
{{verb|take|takes|took|taken|taking}}

