{{documentation subpage}}
<!-- Categories, interwikis and TemplateData go at the bottom of this page. -->
This template is used on template documentation subpages to add a notice at the top of the page and add them to [[:Category:Template documentation pages]].

== Usage ==
<pre>
{{documentation subpage
| 1 = Parent page
| override = The sub-page name
| defaultsort = The way to sort the page in categories
}}
</pre>
This template is added to the top of template and module documentation pages, and adds a header when on the page itself. Nothing will shown when the documentation page is viewed from the parent template.

== TemplateData ==
{{TemplateDataHeader}}
<templatedata>
{
	"params": {
		"1": {
			"required": false,
			"label": "Main page",
			"type": "string/wiki-page-name",
			"description": "The page name which the template documentation is for."
		},
		"override": {
			"required": false,
			"label": "Sub-page",
			"type": "string",
			"description": "The name of the sub-page that the documentation is on."
		},
		"defaultsort": {
			"required": false,
			"label": "Default sort",
			"type": "string",
			"default": "{{PAGENAME}}",
			"description": "How the page is sorted in the category."
		}
	},
	"description": "Template for identifying template documentation pages."
}
</templatedata>

<includeonly>[[Category:Templates]]</includeonly>

{{documentation subpage}}
<!-- Categories, interwikis and TemplateData go at the bottom of this page. -->
Template for marking out templates that need documentation for and adds them to [[:Category:Templates in need of documentation]].

== Usage ==
<pre>
{{documentation needed
| override = Documentation page's sub-page name
| defaultsort = The way to sort the page in categories
}}
</pre>
This template will only categorize the documentation page and not the parent template.

== TemplateData ==
{{TemplateDataHeader}}
<templatedata>
{
	"params": {
		"override": {
			"required": false,
			"label": "Sub-page name",
			"type": "string",
			"description": "The name of the sub-page that the documentation is on."
		},
		"defaultsort": {
			"required": false,
			"label": "Default sort",
			"description": "How the page should be sorted in categories.",
			"type": "string"
		}
	},
	"description": "Template for marking out templates that needs documentation for."
}
</templatedata>

<includeonly>[[Category:Templates]]</includeonly>

{{maintenance}}
Pages in this category contains [[Wiktionary:Lua|Lua module]] errors.

[[Category:Modules]]

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{IPA|/ˌkʌlpəˈbɪləti/}}
* {{audio|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-culpability.wav|UK}}

== Noun ==
{{noun|2=none}}
# {{uncountable}} '''Culpability''' is the state of being [[responsible]] for something [[negative]], such as a [[crime]].
#: ''Oliver Twist was found [[guilty]] of theft, but the real '''culpability''' was Fagin's''.

{{documentation subpage}}
<!-- Categories, interwikis and TemplateData go at the bottom of this page. -->
This template is used on entry pages that have a similar page on the [[w:Main Page|Simple English Wikipedia]] and links to it in a nice box.

== Usage ==
<pre>
{{wikipedia
| 1 = Page on Wikipedia
| 2 = Second alternative page on Wikipedia
| 3 = Third alternative page on Wikipedia
| 4 = Forth alternative page on Wikipedia
| 5 = Fifth alternative page on Wikipedia
}}
</pre>
This template is placed at the top of entry pages, and generally only the first parameter is used.

Note: The interwiki prefix <code><nowiki>w:</nowiki></code> is not needed, it is automatically added to the link when the page is generated.

