=== Pronunciation ===
* {{IPA|/hɪtʃ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-hitch.ogg|US}}

== Noun ==
{{noun|2=hitches}}
# {{countable}} A '''hitch''' is a device that connects a [[trailer]] or [[wagon]] to the thing pulling it.

== Verb ==
{{verb|hitch|es}}
# {{transitive}} If you '''hitch''' something, you [[pull]] it with a [[jerk]].
#: ''John '''hitched''' up his [[shorts]] and ran.''
# {{transitive}} If you '''hitch''' something to something else, you attach or fasten them together.
#: ''He '''hitched''' a [[wagon]] to his truck.''
# {{informal}} If you get '''hitched''', you get [[married]].

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{IPA|/kreɪz/}}
* {{audio|en-us-craze.ogg|US}}

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# A '''craze''' is a temporary [[passion]] or [[infatuation]] for a new amusement, pursuit, or fashion.
#: ''The Twist was a dance '''craze''' of the early 1960s''.

=== Related words ===
* [[crazy]]

