==Verb==
{{verb|griev|e}}
#{{present participle of|grieve}}
# If you are in '''grieving''', you are very sad for a long time, usually because somebody has died.

===Related words===
*[[grief]]

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{UK}} {{US}} {{IPA|/ɡriːv/}}
* {{audio|en-us-grieve.ogg|US}}

== Verb ==
{{verb|griev|e}}
# If you '''grieve''' over something, you feel very sad about it.

=== Related words ===
* [[grief]]

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{IPA|/prɛˈsti(d)ʒ/|/prəˈsti(d)ʒ/}}
* {{audio|en-us-prestige.ogg|US}}

== Noun ==
{{noun|2=none}}
#'''Prestige''' is the [[quality]] of how good the [[reputation]] of something or someone is.
#: ''Oxford has a university of very high '''prestige'''.''

=== Related words ===
* [[prestigious]]

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{IPA|/ˈbʌnd(ə)l/}}
* {{audio|en-us-bundle.ogg|US}}
* {{hyph|bun|dle}}

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# A '''bundle''' is a [[stack]] of objects that are held together by [[wrap]]ping or [[tie|tying]] them.
#: ''There was a '''bundle''' of gifts left at our doorstep this morning.''
# A '''bundle''' is a [[package]] that is wrapped or tied together so that it is easier to carry.
#: ''I made a '''bundle''' of books so that it is easier to bring it to the [[orphanage]].''
# {{informal}} A '''bundle''' is a stack of [[money]].

== Verb ==
{{verb|bundl|e}}
# When you '''bundle''' things, you wrap or tie them together.
#: ''Carrying all these books individually is quite difficult, how about '''bundling''' them together so that it is easier to carry them?''

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{audio|en-us-bundles.ogg|US}}

== Noun ==
{{noun|bundle}}
# {{plural of|bundle}}

== Verb ==
{{verb|bundl|e}}
# {{third-person singular of|bundle}}

{{wikipedia}}

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{IPA|/brɪˈɡeɪd/}}
* {{audio|en-us-brigade.ogg|US}}

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
