<!-- Categories, interwikis and TemplateData go at the bottom of this page. -->
{{substnotice}}
This template is used to award another editor with a cookie, usually used to thank them for their efforts in changing Wiktionary.

== Usage ==
To use this template, add <code><nowiki>{{subst:cookie}}</nowiki></code> to the talk page of the user you wish to award it to.

This template automatically adds your name by using the [[Help:Magic words|magic word]] "REVISIONUSER" and will replace <nowiki>{{</nowiki>subst:REVISIONUSER}} shown in this template. 

To add an additional message, use the <code>|message=</code> parameter as shown below.<br />
<code><nowiki>{{subst:cookie|message=''This is an additional message that you can add if you'd like.''}}</nowiki></code>

== TemplateData ==
{{TemplateDataHeader}}

<templatedata>
{
	"params": {
		"1": {
			"type": "string/wiki-user-name",
			"aliases": [
				"name"
			],
			"default": "Somebody",
			"label": "User name",
			"description": "The name of the user giving the cookie."
		},
		"message": {
			"type": "string",
			"label": "Additional message",
			"description": "An additional message to give to the user you are awarding."
		}
	},
	"description": "Template for awarding an editor with a cookie on the talk page."
}
</templatedata>

