== Verb ==
{{verb|execut|e}}
# {{transitive}} When you '''execute''' someone, you [[kill]] someone due to the [[crime]]s that the person has [[commit]]ted. {{syn|lynch}}
#: ''The [[smuggler]] was found [[guilty]] with delivering [[drug]]s across the [[border]] and was '''executed'''.''
# {{transitive}} When you '''execute''' an action, you carry it out.
#: ''The [[soldier]]s '''executed''' the orders given by their [[superior]].''
# {{transitive}} {{computing}} When you '''execute''' a program, you [[start]], [[launch]] or [[run]] it. {{syn|start|launch|run|open}}
#: ''I '''executed''' the program to begin my [[installation]] of the new web [[browser]].''

=== Related words ===
