* {{hyph|punt|er}}

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# {{countable}} A '''punter''' is a person who [[punt]]s.
# {{countable}} A '''punter''' is a person who [[gamble]]s or makes a [[risky]] [[investment]].

[[Category:People]]

==Adjective==
{{adjective}}
# If something is '''enraging''', it makes you feel very, very angry.
#: ''It is hurtful and '''enraging''' to hear these racist songs on radio.''
#: ''The waste of this money is '''enraging''' to all Canadians.''
#: ''It's very '''enraging''' that he goes to jail while the others are free.''
== Verb ==
{{verb|enrag|e}}
# {{present participle of|enrage}}
#: ''The president of Taiwan asked for independence from China, '''enraging''' the communist leadership.''

=== Word parts ===
{{ety-suffix|provision|al}}

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{IPA|/prəˈvɪʒənəl/}}

== Adjective ==
{{adjective}}
# When something is '''provisional''', it is something that is [[temporary]] and may change later.
#: ''I can make a '''provisional''' agreement with you right now until we get more details later.''
#: ''As the original [[government]] was [[overthrow]]n, a '''provisional''' government was set up to take control of the country.''

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# A '''provisional''' refers to a temporary [[stamp]] that is used locally before an official one is [[release]]d.

== Verb ==
{{verb|tell off|tells off|told off|told off|telling off}}
# {{third-person singular of|tell off}}

