# When something or someone is '''participative''', it can [[participate]] or is able to participate in something.

=== Word parts === {{ety-suffix|ripe|en}}
=== Pronunciation === * {{IPA|/ˈraɪpən/}} * {{audio|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ripen.wav|UK}}
== Verb == {{verb}} # {{ti verb}} When a fruit or grain '''ripens''', it becomes softer, sweeter, and ready to eat. #: ''As the summer ends, the grapes '''ripen''' to a perfect sweetness, ideal for picking.'' #: ''Pears, unlike apples, don't taste as good if allowed to '''ripen''' on the tree.'' #: ''The farmer uses a special gas to '''ripen''' the bananas quickly before they go to market.'' # {{ti verb}} When a cheese '''ripens''', it ages under controlled conditions and slowly develops its flavor, texture, and smell. #: ''This type of cheddar '''ripens''' best in a cool, dark room.'' #: ''The cheesemaker carefully controls the temperature and humidity to '''ripen''' the brie.''

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{UK}} {{US}} {{IPA|/əbˈsɛʃən/}}
* {{audio|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-obsession.wav|UK}}

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
