== Noun == {{noun|2=anatomies}} # '''Anatomy''' is a type of [[science]]. It {{r|stud|ies}} the parts that make up living things, including [[plants]], [[animal]]s, and [[human]]s. #: ''He studied for his '''anatomy''' test all night, but still couldn't remember the names of the [[bone]]s in the body, or where all the [[organ]]s are.'' #: ''The '''anatomies''' of [[monkey]] [[brain]]s and human brains are actually very [[similar]].'' # '''Anatomy''' is the inside of something. It is something that you have [[divide]]d up or looked at in very little parts so you can study it, even its smallest [[detail]]s. #: ''After the President was fired, the reporter spent a year working on a book called "The '''Anatomy''' of a {{lc|Political}} {{lc|Scandal}}." She wanted to make sure she included every detail.'' #: ''The documentary "The '''Anatomy''' of Your Favorite Fast Food Restaurant" made me never want to eat fast food again.''
