== Expression == {{expression}} # If something is '''at least''' some amount or level, it is not less than that, but it could be more. {{synonyms|minimum}} #: ''I don't know how much it costs, but it's '''at least''' $10.'' #: ''This will take '''at least''' an hour.'' # You use '''at least''' to suggest that something is the worst or most basic of the acceptable options. {{synonyms|minimum}} #: '''''At least''' she deserves your thanks.'' # You use '''at least''' to focus on a positive part of a bad situation. #: ''It's too bad you broke your arm, but '''at least''' you can still hold things.'' # You use '''at least''' when you want to change, correct, or [[qualify]] something you just said. #: ''It should be easier the second time. '''At least''', that's what they told me.'' #: ''It's pretty easy to find a good school. '''At least''', it is here.''
=== Related words === * [[at]] * [[least]]

