=== Pronunciation ===
* {{UK}} {{IPA|/ˈwəːk.aʊt/}}
* {{audio|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-workout.wav}}
* {{US}} {{IPA|/ˈwɚk.aʊt/}}

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# {{countable}} Any time when a person is exercising.
#: ''Hiking up the mountain was a good '''workout'''.''

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdʒɛtɪsn̩/|/-zn̩/}}
* {{US}} {{IPA|/ˈdʒɛɾɪsn̩/|/-zn̩/}}
* {{AU}} {{IPA|/ˈdʒɛɾəsən/|/ˈdʒɛtɪsən/}}
* {{audio|en-us-jettison.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en-au-jettison.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# A '''jettison''' is the action of [[#Verb|jettison]]ing something from a [[watercraft]] or [[aircraft]].

== Verb ==
{{verb}}

# If you '''jettison''' something, you [[eject]] it from a [[watercraft]] or [[aircraft]] so as to [[reduce]] its [[load]].

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{enPR|ēʹgrĕs}}, {{IPA|/ˈiːɡrɛs/}}
* {{audio|en-us-egress.ogg|US}}
* {{audio|en-au-egress.ogg|AU}}

== Noun ==
{{noun|egress|egresses}}
# An '''egress''' is an [[exit]].
#: ''The window provides an '''egress''' in the event of an [[emergency]].'' <!--from en.wikt-->

== Verb ==
{{verb|egress|es}}
# {{intransitive}} If you '''egress''', you [[leave]] or [[exit]] a place.

=== Pronunciation ===
* {{UK}} {{IPA|/kəˈmɛnʃərət/}}
* {{US}} {{IPA|/kəˈmɛnsərət/}}
