== Expression ==
{{expression}}
# '''Buridan's ass''' is a [[philosophical]] [[question]] that can be [[summarized]] like this: A hungry ass ([[donkey]]) is placed in between two [[bale]]s of [[hay]]. Both bales of hay are equally far from the donkey, and both bales are completely [[identical]] and [[equally]] good. The donkey needs to eat at least one of the bales of hay, otherwise it will [[starve]] and [[die]]. Assuming that [[free will]] does not exist and that the donkey decides purely based on [[logic]], how does the donkey decide which hay bale to eat? If it decides to eat both of them, how does it choose which one to eat first?

[[Category:Paradoxes]]
[[Category:Philosophy]]
[[Category:Eponyms]]

