# The '''collective''' amount or results are those when all the various parts are brought together.
#: ''When we each contributed what we had, the '''collective''' amount was $313.23.''

== Noun ==
{{noun}}
# {{countable}} A '''collective''' is a group of people with a shared goal.
#: ''The band is a '''collective''' of musicians from across Canada.''
# {{countable}} A '''collective''' is kind of business owned by a group of people, often its workers, customers, or suppliers. {{syn|cooperative}}
#: ''She helped set up a writers' '''collective''' so independent writers could join and get health insurance.''
# {{countable}} A '''collective''' is a word that refers to a group of one type of thing, often animals.
#: ''The '''collective''' noun for fish is "a school of fish".''

